Result:
I found 10 problems, all in the new guard. Eight are ways to get a destructive command past it and two are small cleanups. I confirmed each bypass by calling `guard()` directly in node. The worst one makes the hook time out, and the hook then lets the command through. I did not run `npm run check` or `claude plugin validate`.

